    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Trea Turner** (81.27) and **Kyle Schwarber** (79.18) acting as our offensive anchors, both benefiting from a highly favorable matchup against Mor\u00e1n. The combination of Mor\u00e1n\u2019s mediocre 4.52 xERA and the boost from their respective spots at the top of the order creates an ideal environment for runs and counting stats. While **Junior Caminero** (70.52) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.07) are also strong plays, the latter is a standout efficiency pick today; despite hitting ninth, his +14% platoon edge against Holmes, G is the primary driver in his elevated score, confirming his role as a high-upside play in a favorable matchup.\n\nStrategic benching remains critical to our category dominance, particularly in our quest to mitigate the scarcity of stolen bases. **Chase Meidroth** (47.77) was the toughest exclusion from the starting nine, but he ultimately yielded to the superior matchup-based projections of **Luke Raley** (60.89), who faces Imai\u2019s generous 5.79 xERA. We are maintaining a strict adherence to our 40.0 efficiency floor, which necessitated the benching of **Caleb Durbin** (39.67) and **Dillon Dingler** (37.92); both lacked the necessary combination of park factor and SP vulnerability to warrant a start. We will continue to monitor the status of **Kazuma Okamoto** (58.89), as he faces a tougher challenge against McClanahan, but his power profile provides enough baseline utility to keep him in the lineup despite the challenging 3.97 xERA.",
